This looks like September 2011. The VIX near 39 and the 10-year yield near 1.99% fit the August–September 2011 selloff after the US debt-ceiling downgrade. Long Treasuries are up 13% in one month, and gold fell 11% in a month, which fits late September 2011. Unemployment at 9.1% and headline CPI at 3.76% (roughly 3.9% in September) both match. Emerging-market equity dropped 18% in the month, which also fits September 2011.

Gold peaked in early September 2011 and then fell, so a 1-month drop of 11% points to the end of September. The 10-year yield was about 1.92% at the end of September, and the snapshot's 1.99% is close to that.

